mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;background:rgb(217,217,217);">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:12.0000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">4.教学内容及进度安排</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">/Course Content & Schedule</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:12.0000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">（</font></span><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Courier New';font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">按照教学周编排，应包含每节课教学内容及教学目标，如有作业及考核要求，请一并列明）</font></span><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:12.0000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:176.7000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><strong>第1周</strong></p>
<p>绪论</p>
<p>学习物理化学的任务和内容、物理化学的发展及其与药学的关系和物理化学的学习方法。</p>
<p>第一章 热力学第一定律</p>
<p>学习热力学概论、热力学的一些基本概念、体积功和可逆过程、热力学第一定律概述、焓和热容。</p>
<p><strong>第2周</strong></p>
<p>第一章 热力学第一定律</p>
<p>学习热力学第一定律的应用、热化学和几种热效应。</p>
<p>第二章、热力学第二定律</p>
<p>学习热力学第二定律概述、卡诺循环和卡诺定理、熵函数及过程方向性的判据、熵变的计算、热力学第三定律概述。</p>
<p><strong>第3周</strong></p>
<p>第二章、热力学第二定律</p>
<p>学习亥姆霍兹和吉布斯自由能、亥姆霍兹自由能变和吉布斯自由能变的计算、热力学函数间的关系、非平衡态热力学简介</p>
<p>第三章、多组分系统热力学</p>
<p>学习多组分系统和组成表示法、偏摩尔量、化学势、稀溶液的两个经验定律</p>
<p><strong>第4周</strong></p>
<p>第三章、多组分系统热力学</p>
<p>学习气体混合物中各组分的化学势、液体混合物、稀溶液、真实溶液中组分的化学势、稀溶液的依数性和分配定律。</p>
<p><strong>第5周</strong></p>
<p>第四章 化学平衡</p>
<p>学习化学反应的吉布斯自由能变化和平衡条件、化学反应等温方程式与标准平衡常数、平衡常数表示法、平衡常数测定和平衡转化率的计算、标准反应吉布斯能变化及化合物的标准生成吉布斯能、温度对平衡常数的影响、其他因素对平衡的影响、反应的耦合。</p>
<p><strong>第6周</strong></p>
<p>第五章 相平衡</p>
<p>学习相律及其基本概念、单组分系统、完全互溶双液系统、部分完全互溶双液系统和完全不部分完全互溶双液系统。</p>
<p><strong>第7周</strong></p>
<p>第五章 相平衡</p>
<p>学习两组分固-液系统、三组分系统。</p>
<p>第六章、电化学</p>
<p>学习法拉第电解定律和离子的电迁移、电解质溶液电导和测定、强电解质溶液的活度和活度系数、可逆电池和可逆电池热力学。</p>
<p><strong>第8周</strong></p>
<p>第六章 电化学</p>
<p>学习标准氢电极和电极电势、浓差电池、电池电动势的应用、电解与电极的极化和生物电化学。</p>
<p><strong>第9周</strong></p>
<p>第七章 化学动力学</p>
<p>学习化学反应速率和化学反应速率方程、具有简单级数反应、温度对反应速率的影响几种、几种典型的复杂反应</p>
<p><strong>第10周</strong></p>
<p>第七章 化学动力学</p>
<p>学习链反应及其速率方程、反应速率理论、溶液中的反应、光化学和催化反应</p>
<p>第十章 大分子溶液</p>
<p>学习大分子及大分子溶液的基本特性、大分子溶液的流变性、大分子溶液的超离心沉降和凝胶。</p>
<p><strong>第11周</strong></p>
<p>学习表面吉布斯能、表面张力以及表面的热力学关系式、弯曲表面的性质、溶液的表面吸附、铺展与浸润、不溶性表面膜、表面活性剂、固体在溶液中的吸附。</p>
<p><strong>第12周</strong></p>
<p>第九章 胶体分散系统</p>
<p>学习溶胶分散系统及其制备、溶胶的动力学性质、溶胶的光学性质、溶胶的电学性质、溶胶的溶胶的稳定性和聚沉、乳状液及微乳状液。</p>
<p><strong>第17周</strong></p>
<p>考试。</p>
<p><strong>第18周</strong></p>
<p>阅卷和评分。</p>
<p><strong>Week 1</strong><br><strong>Introduction</strong><br>Tasks and content of physical chemistry, its development, relationship with pharmacy, and learning methodologies.</p>
<p><strong>Chapter 1: The First Law of Thermodynamics</strong><br>Overview of thermodynamics, basic concepts, volume work and reversible processes, the first law of thermodynamics, enthalpy and heat capacity.</p>
<p><strong>Week 2</strong><br><strong>Chapter 1: The First Law of Thermodynamics (Continued)</strong><br>Applications of the first law, thermochemistry, and various thermal effects.</p>
<p><strong>Chapter 2: The Second Law of Thermodynamics</strong><br>Overview of the second law, Carnot cycle and theorem, entropy function and criteria for process directionality, entropy change calculations, overview of the third law of thermodynamics.</p>
<p><strong>Week 3</strong><br><strong>Chapter 2: The Second Law of Thermodynamics (Continued)</strong><br>Helmholtz and Gibbs free energy, calculations of Helmholtz and Gibbs free energy changes, relationships between thermodynamic functions, introduction to non-equilibrium thermodynamics.</p>
<p><strong>Chapter 3: Thermodynamics of Multicomponent Systems</strong><br>Multicomponent systems and composition representation, partial molar quantities, chemical potential, two empirical laws of dilute solutions.</p>
<p><strong>Week 4</strong><br><strong>Chapter 3: Thermodynamics of Multicomponent Systems (Continued)</strong><br>Chemical potential of components in gas mixtures, liquid mixtures, dilute solutions, chemical potential of components in real solutions, colligative properties of dilute solutions, and distribution law.</p>
<p><strong>Week 5</strong><br><strong>Chapter 4: Chemical Equilibrium</strong><br>Gibbs free energy change and equilibrium conditions for chemical reactions, reaction isotherm and standard equilibrium constant, representations of equilibrium constants, determination of equilibrium constants and calculation of equilibrium conversion rates, standard Gibbs free energy change and standard formation Gibbs free energy of compounds, effect of temperature on equilibrium constants, influence of other factors on equilibrium, coupled reactions.</p>
<p><strong>Week 6</strong><br><strong>Chapter 5: Phase Equilibrium</strong><br>Phase rule and basic concepts, single-component systems, completely miscible binary liquid systems, partially miscible and completely immiscible binary liquid systems.</p>
<p><strong>Week 7</strong><br><strong>Chapter 5: Phase Equilibrium (Continued)</strong><br>Binary solid-liquid systems, ternary systems.</p>
<p><strong>Chapter 6: Electrochemistry</strong><br>Faraday's laws of electrolysis and ion migration, conductivity of electrolyte solutions and its measurement, activity and activity coefficients of strong electrolyte solutions, reversible cells and thermodynamics of reversible cells.</p>
<p><strong>Week 8</strong><br><strong>Chapter 6: Electrochemistry (Continued)</strong><br>Standard hydrogen electrode and electrode potential, concentration cells, applications of cell electromotive force, electrolysis and electrode polarization, bioelectrochemistry.</p>
<p><strong>Week 9</strong><br><strong>Chapter 7: Chemical Kinetics</strong><br>Reaction rates and rate equations, reactions with simple orders, effect of temperature on reaction rates, several typical complex reactions.</p>
<p><strong>Week 10</strong><br><strong>Chapter 7: Chemical Kinetics (Continued)</strong><br>Chain reactions and their rate equations, reaction rate theories, reactions in solutions, photochemistry and catalytic reactions.</p>
<p><strong>Chapter 10: Macromolecular Solutions</strong><br>Basic characteristics of macromolecules and macromolecular solutions, rheology of macromolecular solutions, ultracentrifugal sedimentation of macromolecular solutions, and gels.</p>
<p><strong>Week 11</strong><br>Surface Gibbs energy, surface tension and thermodynamic relationships of surfaces, properties of curved surfaces, surface adsorption of solutions, spreading and wetting, insoluble surface films, surfactants, adsorption of solids in solutions.</p>
<p><strong>Week 12</strong><br><strong>Chapter 9: Colloidal Dispersion Systems</strong><br>Preparation of colloidal dispersion systems, kinetic properties of colloids, optical properties of colloids, electrical properties of colloids, stability and coagulation of colloids, emulsions and microemulsions.</p>
<p><strong>Week 17</strong><br>Examinations.</p>
<p><strong>Week 18</strong><br>Grading and evaluation.</p></font></span><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
